+# Tasks: Simplify Physics Bookkeeping
+
+**Input**: [spec.md](spec.md), [plan.md](plan.md), [research.md](research.md), [data-model.md](data-model.md), [physics contract](contracts/physics-lifecycle.md), [evidence contract](contracts/validation-evidence.md), and [quickstart.md](quickstart.md).
+
+**Prerequisites**: Read those artifacts and `.specify/memory/constitution.md`. The active feature is `specs/003-simplify-physics-bookkeeping`; preserve the actual Git branch and user changes. All tasks below are pending. Paths are repository-relative unless a capture manifest records an absolute external path.
+
+**Tests**: Explicitly required by the specification. Add missing characterization before changing the relevant implementation, and establish the expected passing behavior on the baseline. This is an observationally equivalent refactor: do not manufacture a failing behavior test simply to satisfy the sample template's red-test wording. Use independent expected physical results and lifecycle histories, not a mirror of a private helper.
+
+**Organization**: Setup → foundation → US2 state reductions → US1 code readability → US3 confidence/evidence → completion and maintainer review. All three stories are P1. The order follows the plan's shared-file and final-walkthrough dependencies, rather than pretending these refactors can safely edit the same runtime concurrently.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story?] Description`
+
+- Every task has an unchecked box, sequential ID and concrete file/output paths.
+- `[P]` means the task may run alongside its explicitly listed peer after their common prerequisite, with distinct file ownership. It does not authorize extra agents by itself or override measurement/resource isolation.
+- Story-phase tasks have `[US1]`, `[US2]` or `[US3]`; setup, foundation and polish tasks have no story label.
+- Evidence paths are outputs to create, not proof already collected. Large raw captures may live in a fresh ignored `bin/physics-bookkeeping.*` directory with exact location, source snapshots, manifests and checksums recorded in feature evidence.
+
+## Phase 1: Setup (Preserve the Current Baseline)
+
+**Purpose**: Establish equivalent source, build and measurement infrastructure before runtime edits. The historical commit is context, not the performance or behavioral control.
+
+- [ ] T001 Record actual HEAD, dirty tracked/untracked changes, toolchain, dependency/build options, CPU topology/governor, worker counts/affinity and initial scope in `specs/003-simplify-physics-bookkeeping/evidence/baseline-provenance.md`; compare current physics/lifecycle code with planned baseline `f6d1af73fcb9a9e623b735fe0a8269d6e65c8fba` and historical `79069591488a68223f8e71ce5f24ddf2d37fb609`, update stale assumptions, verify existing ignore rules protect new raw captures, and preserve existing user artifacts without changing checklist markers.
