+## Implementation Strategy
+
+1. Preserve and characterize the current engine before simplifying it. Build/test scaffolding may be shared with the isolated baseline, with patches and fingerprints recorded; keep all physical fixture/runtime changes distinguishable.
+2. Deliver US2 as the smallest substantive technical MVP: support identities and queue index replace redundant facts. It is independently testable and materially simplifies state without requiring new classes or the geometry extraction.
+3. Complete US1 with direct participation rules, explicit geometry inputs, concise local invariants and all eight final walkthroughs. Naming and file moves supplement the state reductions; they cannot replace them.
+4. Complete US3 on the final runtime: focused/full/public checks, probes/safety, separate physical validation and isolated matched timing, then investigate regressions. Reuse coverage rather than building a second verification framework.
+5. Finish reviewable code/evidence before the maintainer walkthrough. Report independently completed technical work while human review is pending; mark full acceptance only after the actual review and any resulting fixes are verified.
+
+**Inventory**: 43 tasks total: setup 4; foundation 3; US2 11; US1 9; US3 11; polish/human acceptance 5. Ten `[P]` tasks form five explicit parallel pairs. All 43 tasks are pending; no implementation check or human judgment is implied by task generation.
